{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(Cross_Sections)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(Cross Sections)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The circular base of a hemisphere of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rests on the base of a square pyramid of height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The hemisphere is tangent to the other four faces of the pyramid. What is the edge-length of the base of the pyramid?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/4/794b804e8ea5c3f8c1a08f50ef63d6fdf5f6f91b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{13}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4\\sqrt{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{13}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"422\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> be the pyramid with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> as the square base. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and the midpoint of side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Lastly, let the hemisphere be tangent to the triangular face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d9053237c11f93476d03e5e8384171c727b8784a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EOM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> has a right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since the hemisphere is tangent to the triangular face <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd85454c0ce4000c0e63b4a1c4a12ef6f8b56e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2110e5c2b850f0153ec6fd5bb97df45f3fe988d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EPO$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d9053237c11f93476d03e5e8384171c727b8784a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EOM$\" width=\"64\" height=\"13\" /> is similar to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4ce92facedcf972df801b9718ab05594f6c366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EPO$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e049bc5b3169976b9d2be4e4fbae3fd408dcc5f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{OM}{2} = \\frac{6}{EP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"93\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ec7e39c018daa87c3269ef81769c5ff70e3d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = \\frac{6}{EP} \\times 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c325e4d89cf25b85e3a844054a60cecc26c4caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OM = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6^2 - 2^2}} \\times 2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"224\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>The length of the square base is thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cf3d4d75bd2eec6832a97a7247b4c7d16a2a79a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 3\\sqrt{2} \\rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"180\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a cross section of the pyramid such that it is a hemisphere inscribed inside of a triangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the vertex furthest away from the hemisphere. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be a point where the hemisphere is tangent. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the centre of the hemisphere. Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65d6fe768733942de7abb4a750badc3527cb5be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AOP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is a right triangle, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is ninety degrees. Apply the pythagorean formula to find side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b453efc0779bc8d105a2fdad8729864a6d34cf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\sqrt{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"40\" height=\"21\" /> Since we know the answer must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4dc1409208ff6a3039f4871d85c16763334983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"26\" height=\"21\" /> somewhere, we can remove choices B, D and E from selection. Choice C is simply the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, which cannot be the desired length. Thus, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc308ff37f94838c11808d9746f10ba1ac15deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ jaspersun\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3.28Cross_Sections.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(Cross_Sections)\">Solution 3(Cross Sections)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(Cross Sections)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The cross section of this entire figure is just an isosceles triangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and a semicircle tangent to the congruent sides of the triangle and its base is on the base of the triangle. This semicircle has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now draw the line connecting the center of this semicircle and the point of tangency with one of the sides. This will have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Let the hypotenuse of this new right triangle we just created have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the altitude of the isosceles triangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> will be similar to this triangle with hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Hence, the hypotenuse of this longer triangle is just <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e772565177713df9b031853ab3d1de84d451df4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{36 + x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"21\" />. By similar triangles\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6341c20712d976eb23527676d88c7c2ae23d3f80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{6} = \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{36 + x^2}} \\implies \\sqrt{36 + x^2} = 3x \\implies 36 + x^2 = 9x^2 \\implies x^2 = \\frac{36}{8} = \\frac{9}{2} \\implies x = \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"715\" height=\"48\" />. Since this is only a half of the base of the isosceles triangle, we double <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to get\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc308ff37f94838c11808d9746f10ba1ac15deb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{A}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~ilikemath247365\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u23iWcqbJlE\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=u23iWcqbJlE</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A\">2011 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017224231\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.061 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 318/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7827/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n10